# 12. THE FOUR-MISSION HOLDOUT RESULT IS WAY TOO SMALL TO LEAN ON

You write:

> “A four-mission hold-out has high-risk MAE 19.2 on a single held-out high-risk event.”

That's effectively **n = 1** for the high-risk metric. 

Don't make this sound like substantial validation.

I would either:

**A. Expand it**, if possible.

or

**B. Put it clearly in an exploratory appendix.**

Something like:

> “The mission-level holdout contained one high-risk event, so high-risk conclusions from this analysis are not statistically interpretable.”

That sentence protects you.

